# Copy this file to `.env` (gitignored -- never commit the real one, it's
# meant to carry values specific to wherever you're actually deploying this)
# and fill in real values. `docker compose up` works with zero .env at all --
# every variable below has a sane default for local/testing use; this file
# only matters once you need to change one of them (e.g. to avoid colliding
# with another service's ports on a shared host, or to front the enrollment
# endpoint with Traefik via docker-compose.proxy.yml).

# --- Host-side port overrides (docker-compose.yml) --------------------------
# Only needed if the defaults collide with something else already running on
# the same Docker host. Container-internal ports are fixed (see src/app.rs)
# and unaffected by these.
# MICROTAK_ENROLLMENT_HOST_PORT=8446
# MICROTAK_MARTI_API_HOST_PORT=8443
# MICROTAK_PLAIN_TCP_HOST_PORT=8087
# MICROTAK_MTLS_HOST_PORT=8089

# --- Traefik overlay (docker-compose.proxy.yml) -----------------------------
# Only needed if you're using docker-compose.proxy.yml.
# The public hostname clients will reach the enrollment endpoint at.
# MICROTAK_DOMAIN=microtak.example.com
# The external Docker network your existing Traefik instance is attached to.
# TRAEFIK_NETWORK=web
# The Traefik entrypoint (as named in Traefik's own static config) that
# terminates TLS for this router.
# TRAEFIK_ENROLLMENT_ENTRYPOINT=websecure
# The certResolver (as named in Traefik's own static config) that issues the
# real certificate for MICROTAK_DOMAIN.
# TRAEFIK_CERT_RESOLVER=letsencrypt
